#X text 240 108 Typical use cases:;
#X text 250 133 • Automatic keyboard backlight control — adjusting
the backlight brightness from a patch \, for example reducing it during
a performance or matching it to the ambient light in the room.;
#X text 250 203 • Reacting to sound with the backlight — using the
keyboard backlight as a simple visual indicator that follows the sound
\, for example pulsing in time with the music or brightening on loud
moments.;
